  "decision": [
    "Delete the numeric compatibility ID list without a replacement table: the existing Quantity policy grammar fixes overflow=refuse and rounding=none. Retain Runtime profile numeric_law binding.",
    "Select the typed profile uniquely by its declared role and actual admission law; preserve owner and closure checks without a fixed profile ID.",
    "Derive structured constructor roles from existing closed value-rule variants, preserving profile-owner export completeness and uniqueness without fixed constructor IDs.",
    "Use the existing stage/signal reason mechanism for the four distinct static structured faults, retaining unique reason and diagnostic ownership."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The renamed graphs fail admission and do not produce renamed RIRs. Their public failures are startup/admission evidence, not admitted renamed Experiment execution.",
    "The original numeric baseline public build/check/run exits 0; raw subprocess receipts are under baseline/cli-results.json.",
    "The unified correction is not implemented by this evidence record. A corrected Kernel requires truthful re-identification, affected conformance and actual maintained-input revalidation before the final build freeze."
  ]
}
